# Web App – Next.js App Router

Read `docs/WEB.md` (the design handoff: boards, layouts, rules) and `docs/web/PLAN.md` (architecture and build order) before building a screen. The canvas boards are the spec; `docs/redesign/tokens.md` and `glossary.md` hold values and words.

## Data

- **The web is a Supabase client like the phone.** It reads and writes Postgres directly under RLS with the publishable key. There are no API route handlers for app data, and none may be added: secret-key operations (account deletion, QR sign-in) are Supabase Edge Functions both apps call, and AI goes to the Go backend.
- Synced rows are soft-deleted (`deleted = true`), never `DELETE`d, or phones never learn of the delete.
- Never sum across currencies; money is `MinorAmount` from `@repo/types`.
- Ledger data loads into the browser (the shared store, `docs/adr/0003-web-shares-the-legend-state-store.md`); only the landing page, auth and the shell render on the server.
- Domain rules come from workspace packages, never re-typed in `apps/web`. Add each package to `transpilePackages` in `next.config.js`.
- DB types: `import type { Database } from '@repo/types/database'` (generated, `pnpm gen:db-types`).

## Structure

```
src/proxy.ts                    session refresh + private-path redirect (Next 16 name for middleware)
src/lib/routes.ts               public paths, safe `next` redirects
src/lib/supabase/client.ts      browser client (cookies via @supabase/ssr)
src/lib/supabase/server.ts      Server Components / route handlers
src/app/auth/callback/route.ts  PKCE exchange (Google, email links)
```

A new public route (landing, legal, the public deletion page) goes in `PUBLIC_PATHS` in `src/lib/routes.ts` with a test case.

## Supabase clients

- `@/lib/supabase/server` in Server Components and route handlers; `@/lib/supabase/client` in client components.
- In `proxy.ts`, nothing runs between `createServerClient` and `auth.getClaims()`.
- Never use the secret key (`sb_secret_...`) anywhere in `apps/web`.

## Testing

- Vitest for web modules (`pnpm --filter web test`): call the interface with literal inputs, assert literal outputs.
- Playwright drives the real app for each screen at 1440, 1024, 820 and 390 wide against the board renders.
- CI runs `next build`, so a prerender failure fails the job.
